{
  "_comment": [
    "Record from two 32-channel RHD2132/Omnetics broadband sources at the same time.",
    "Topology: two kBroadbandSource -> one kApplication (stateful-decode-and-sync) -> one kDiskWriter.",
    "",
    "PERIPHERAL IDs: a kBroadbandSource node BINDS an existing device Peripheral by its",
    "unique device-assigned peripheral_id; it does not create or clone one. Two nodes",
    "therefore cannot both be 'peripheral_id 200' -- the second physical device enumerates",
    "as its own ID. Source 1 uses the current bench Omnetics ID (200). Source 2 uses a",
    "placeholder (201) that MUST be replaced with the real second ID reported by",
    "'synapsectl -u <ip> info' before deployment (per AGENTS.md: do not hard-code a",
    "Synapse peripheral ID).",
    "",
    "UNPROVEN CAPABILITIES to confirm with Science before relying on this file (see",
    "docs/t19-synapse-multisource-capability-audit.md):",
    "  1. Whether one SciFi-2 can enumerate two independent 32-ch Omnetics broadband",
    "     peripherals simultaneously (the recorded inventory only ever showed one, ID 200).",
    "  2. Whether one kApplication supports two upstream readers -- the current App uses a",
    "     single setup_reader()/data_reader_, and NodeConnection carries no input-port field,",
    "     so the two inbound edges (1->3, 2->3) are distinguishable only by src node id.",
    "  3. Whether one kDiskWriter accepts fan-in from two sources and how per-source identity",
    "     and timing are represented in the HDF5 file. If any of these is unsupported, split",
    "     into per-source App/DiskWriter chains or record via the host fusion recorder."
  ],
